IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nz-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `nz-part2-commencement-repeal`

-- Tests for nz-part2-commencement-repeal.l4 (ss 29 to 38).
-- Every expected value was decided by reading the section quoted beside it BEFORE the module was run.

§ `Section 29 -- Power to make commencement order`

-- src:234 | includes a power to state a time of commencement on the date that is set; and
#ASSERT `an Order in Council may state a time of commencement on the date that is set` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `an Order in Council may state a time of commencement on the date that is set` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- src:235 | is capable of being exercised more than once to amend, revoke, or replace an Order in Council made in a previous exercise of the power, so long as each re-exercise of the power takes effect before the commencement takes effect; and
-- A re-exercise taking effect the day before the commencement takes effect: allowed.
#ASSERT `a commencement order may be amended, revoked or replaced by a re-exercise of the power taking effect on` (Date 30 6 2026) `when the commencement takes effect on` (Date 1 7 2026) `and` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- On the same day, with no stated time: commencement takes effect at the start of the day (s 27), so the re-exercise is not before it.
#ASSERT `a commencement order may be amended, revoked or replaced by a re-exercise of the power taking effect on` (Date 1 7 2026) `when the commencement takes effect on` (Date 1 7 2026) `and` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- On the same day, the order states a time and the re-exercise takes effect before that time: before.
#ASSERT `a commencement order may be amended, revoked or replaced by a re-exercise of the power taking effect on` (Date 1 7 2026) `when the commencement takes effect on` (Date 1 7 2026) `and` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- After the commencement: not allowed, whatever the stated time.
#ASSERT `a commencement order may be amended, revoked or replaced by a re-exercise of the power taking effect on` (Date 2 7 2026) `when the commencement takes effect on` (Date 1 7 2026) `and` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `a commencement order may be amended, revoked or replaced by a re-exercise of the power taking effect on` (Date 2 7 2026) `when the commencement takes effect on` (Date 1 7 2026) `and` TRUE EQUALS FALSE

-- src:236 | includes a power to make 1 or more orders setting different dates for different provisions of the legislation; and
#ASSERT `orders may set different dates for different provisions` 0 TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `orders may set different dates for different provisions` 1 TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `orders may set different dates for different provisions` 3 TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `orders may set different dates for different provisions` 2 FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- src:237 | includes (if there is a provision where its commencement would otherwise operate to give effect to other parts of legislation) a power to commence the provision only for the purpose of giving effect to some, but not other, parts of that legislation.
-- src:238 | Example
-- src:239 | The Dogs and Cats Act 2020 states that it comes into force on a date set by Order in Council. Section 100 states that the legislation set out in Schedule 4 is consequentially amended (and Schedule 4 sets out all the amendments). An Order in Council is made that commences section 100 on 1 July 2020 for the purpose of giving effect to the first 10 consequential amendments in Schedule 4. The rest of the consequential amendments in Schedule 4 do not come into force at that time. A later Order in Council commences section 100 for the purpose of the rest of the consequential amendments on 1 July 2021.
-- The Dogs and Cats Act 2020 example: section 100 (consequential amendments in Schedule 4) is commenced on 1 July 2020 only for the purpose of giving effect to the first 10 amendments,
-- and on 1 July 2021 for the rest. Section 100's commencement would otherwise give effect to other parts of legislation (the whole of Schedule 4), so each order uses the power in (1)(d).
#ASSERT `what comes into force when an order commences a provision` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `The provision comes into force only for the stated purpose, and only the identified parts come into force`
-- An order that commences the provision without limiting its purpose brings the whole provision into force.
#ASSERT `what comes into force when an order commences a provision` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `The whole provision comes into force`
#ASSERT `what comes into force when an order commences a provision` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `The whole provision comes into force`
-- A limited-purpose order for a provision whose commencement would not give effect to other parts of legislation is outside the power: the text does not say what happens.
#ASSERT `what comes into force when an order commences a provision` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Section 29(1)(d) gives no such power here: the text does not say what the order does`

§ `Section 30 -- Amendments part of, and construed with, legislation amended`

-- src:242 | 30 Amendments part of, and construed with, legislation amended
-- src:243 | Amending legislation is part of the legislation that it amends.
-- src:244 | Amending legislation must be construed with the legislation that it amends.
#ASSERT `amending legislation is part of the legislation that it amends` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `amending legislation is part of the legislation that it amends` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `amending legislation must be construed with the legislation that it amends` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `amending legislation must be construed with the legislation that it amends` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Section 31 -- References to repeal or amendment extend to other ceasing of effect`

-- src:245 | 31 References to repeal or amendment extend to other ceasing of effect
-- src:246 | A reference in sections 32 to 36, 38, and 39 to repealing or amending legislation includes a reference to—
-- src:247 | an implied repeal or amendment; and
-- src:248 | a change that removes or limits the effect of the legislation; and
-- src:249 | a change that disapplies the legislation to any person, subject matter, or circumstance.
-- The sections it reaches: 32 to 36, 38 and 39. Test each side of both ends and the gap at 37.
#ASSERT `section 31 reaches section` 31 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `section 31 reaches section` 32 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `section 31 reaches section` 34 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `section 31 reaches section` 36 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `section 31 reaches section` 37 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `section 31 reaches section` 38 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `section 31 reaches section` 39 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `section 31 reaches section` 40 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `a change counts as repealing or amending legislation in section` 32 `when the change is` `an express repeal` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a change counts as repealing or amending legislation in section` 33 `when the change is` `an express amendment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a change counts as repealing or amending legislation in section` 34 `when the change is` `an implied repeal or amendment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a change counts as repealing or amending legislation in section` 35 `when the change is` `a change that removes or limits the effect of the legislation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a change counts as repealing or amending legislation in section` 35 `when the change is` `a change that removes the effect of the legislation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a change counts as repealing or amending legislation in section` 35 `when the change is` `a change that limits the effect of the legislation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a change counts as repealing or amending legislation in section` 36 `when the change is` `a change that disapplies the legislation to a person, subject matter or circumstance` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a change counts as repealing or amending legislation in section` 38 `when the change is` `an implied repeal or amendment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a change counts as repealing or amending legislation in section` 39 `when the change is` `a change that removes or limits the effect of the legislation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a change counts as repealing or amending legislation in section` 39 `when the change is` `a change that removes the effect of the legislation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a change counts as repealing or amending legislation in section` 39 `when the change is` `a change that limits the effect of the legislation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A change of another kind: section 31 does not extend to it.
-- Constituents of the printed items (ruling C): each is on the list in every section s 31 reaches.
#ASSERT `a change counts as repealing or amending legislation in section` 32 `when the change is` `an implied repeal` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a change counts as repealing or amending legislation in section` 33 `when the change is` `an implied amendment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a change counts as repealing or amending legislation in section` 34 `when the change is` `a change that disapplies the legislation to a person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a change counts as repealing or amending legislation in section` 35 `when the change is` `a change that disapplies the legislation to a subject matter` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a change counts as repealing or amending legislation in section` 36 `when the change is` `a change that disapplies the legislation to a circumstance` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a change counts as repealing or amending legislation in section` 38 `when the change is` `an implied repeal` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a change counts as repealing or amending legislation in section` 39 `when the change is` `an implied amendment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a change counts as repealing or amending legislation in section` 32 `when the change is` `a change of another kind` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Section 37 is not named: section 31 does not decide it.
#ASSERT `a change counts as repealing or amending legislation in section` 37 `when the change is` `an implied repeal or amendment` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a change counts as repealing or amending legislation in section` 40 `when the change is` `an implied repeal or amendment` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 32 -- Effect of repeal or amendment generally`

-- src:250 | 32 Effect of repeal or amendment generally
-- src:251 | The repeal or amendment of legislation does not—
-- src:252 | affect the validity, invalidity, effect, or consequences of anything done or suffered:
-- src:253 | affect an existing right, interest, title, immunity, duty, status, or capacity:
-- src:254 | affect an amendment made by the legislation to other legislation:
-- src:255 | affect the previous operation of the legislation or anything done or suffered under it:
-- src:256 | revive any thing that is not in force or existing at the time the repeal or amendment takes effect.
-- src:257 | The repeal of legislation does not revive—
-- src:258 | legislation that has been repealed; or
-- src:259 | a rule of law that has been abolished.
#ASSERT `a repeal or amendment of legislation does this, under section 32` `affects the validity, invalidity, effect or consequences of anything done or suffered` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a repeal or amendment of legislation does this, under section 32` `affects an existing right, interest, title, immunity, duty, status or capacity` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a repeal or amendment of legislation does this, under section 32` `affects an amendment made by the legislation to other legislation` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a repeal or amendment of legislation does this, under section 32` `affects the previous operation of the legislation or anything done or suffered under it` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a repeal or amendment of legislation does this, under section 32` `revives a thing that is not in force or existing when the repeal or amendment takes effect` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a repeal or amendment of legislation does this, under section 32` `revives a thing that is not in force when the repeal or amendment takes effect` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a repeal or amendment of legislation does this, under section 32` `revives a thing that is not existing when the repeal or amendment takes effect` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a repeal or amendment of legislation does this, under section 32` `revives legislation that has been repealed` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a repeal or amendment of legislation does this, under section 32` `revives a rule of law that has been abolished` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Constituents of the printed items (ruling C): section 32(1) says the repeal or amendment does none of these.
#ASSERT `a repeal or amendment of legislation does this, under section 32` `affects the validity of anything done or suffered` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a repeal or amendment of legislation does this, under section 32` `affects the invalidity of anything done or suffered` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a repeal or amendment of legislation does this, under section 32` `affects the effect of anything done or suffered` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a repeal or amendment of legislation does this, under section 32` `affects the consequences of anything done or suffered` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a repeal or amendment of legislation does this, under section 32` `affects an existing right` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a repeal or amendment of legislation does this, under section 32` `affects an existing interest` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a repeal or amendment of legislation does this, under section 32` `affects an existing title` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a repeal or amendment of legislation does this, under section 32` `affects an existing immunity` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a repeal or amendment of legislation does this, under section 32` `affects an existing duty` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a repeal or amendment of legislation does this, under section 32` `affects an existing status` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a repeal or amendment of legislation does this, under section 32` `affects an existing capacity` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a repeal or amendment of legislation does this, under section 32` `affects the previous operation of the legislation` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a repeal or amendment of legislation does this, under section 32` `affects anything done or suffered under the legislation` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a repeal or amendment of legislation does this, under section 32` `has another effect` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 33 -- Effect of repeal or amendment on existing rights and proceedings`

-- src:260 | 33 Effect of repeal or amendment on existing rights and proceedings
-- src:261 | The repeal or amendment of legislation does not affect—
-- src:262 | the completion of a matter or thing that relates to an existing right, interest, title, immunity, duty, status, or capacity (a legal position); or
-- src:263 | the commencing of a proceeding that relates to an existing legal position; or
-- src:264 | the completion of a proceeding commenced or in progress under the legislation.
-- src:265 | Repealed or amended legislation continues to have effect for the purposes stated in subsection (1) as if the legislation had not been repealed or amended.
#ASSERT `the completion of the matter or thing is unaffected by the repeal or amendment` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the completion of the matter or thing is unaffected by the repeal or amendment` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the commencing of the proceeding is unaffected by the repeal or amendment` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the commencing of the proceeding is unaffected by the repeal or amendment` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the completion of the proceeding is unaffected by the repeal or amendment` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the completion of the proceeding is unaffected by the repeal or amendment` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `repealed or amended legislation continues to have effect for the purposes of section 33(1)` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `repealed or amended legislation continues to have effect for the purposes of section 33(1)` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `repealed or amended legislation continues to have effect for the purposes of section 33(1)` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `repealed or amended legislation continues to have effect for the purposes of section 33(1)` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Section 34 -- Effect of repeal or amendment on prior offences and breaches of legislation`

-- src:266 | 34 Effect of repeal or amendment on prior offences and breaches of legislation
-- src:267 | The repeal or amendment of legislation does not affect a liability to a penalty or any other remedy or relief, or to an order or a direction, for an offence or for a breach of any legislation committed before the repeal or amendment.
-- src:268 | Repealed or amended legislation continues to have effect as if it had not been repealed or amended for the purpose of—
-- src:269 | investigating the offence or breach:
-- src:270 | commencing or completing a proceeding for the offence or breach:
-- src:271 | imposing a penalty, or any other remedy or relief, or making or giving an order or a direction, for the offence or breach.
-- (1) An offence on 28 Feb 2026, a repeal taking effect 1 Mar 2026: before, so the liability survives.
#ASSERT `the liability for an offence or breach committed on` (Date 28 2 2026) `is unaffected by a repeal or amendment taking effect on` (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS TRUE
-- Same day: the repeal takes effect at the start of the day (s 39), so the offence is not before it.
#ASSERT `the liability for an offence or breach committed on` (Date 1 3 2026) `is unaffected by a repeal or amendment taking effect on` (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the liability for an offence or breach committed on` (Date 2 3 2026) `is unaffected by a repeal or amendment taking effect on` (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS FALSE
-- (2) each of the three purposes, an offence before and not before the repeal; another purpose is not listed.
#ASSERT `repealed or amended legislation continues to have effect as if not repealed or amended for the purpose of` `investigating the offence or breach` `for an offence or breach committed on` (Date 28 2 2026) `before a repeal or amendment taking effect on` (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `repealed or amended legislation continues to have effect as if not repealed or amended for the purpose of` `commencing or completing a proceeding for the offence or breach` `for an offence or breach committed on` (Date 28 2 2026) `before a repeal or amendment taking effect on` (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `repealed or amended legislation continues to have effect as if not repealed or amended for the purpose of` `imposing a penalty, or any other remedy or relief, or making or giving an order or a direction, for the offence or breach` `for an offence or breach committed on` (Date 28 2 2026) `before a repeal or amendment taking effect on` (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `repealed or amended legislation continues to have effect as if not repealed or amended for the purpose of` `investigating the offence or breach` `for an offence or breach committed on` (Date 1 3 2026) `before a repeal or amendment taking effect on` (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `repealed or amended legislation continues to have effect as if not repealed or amended for the purpose of` `commencing or completing a proceeding for the offence or breach` `for an offence or breach committed on` (Date 2 3 2026) `before a repeal or amendment taking effect on` (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `repealed or amended legislation continues to have effect as if not repealed or amended for the purpose of` `imposing a penalty, or any other remedy or relief, or making or giving an order or a direction, for the offence or breach` `for an offence or breach committed on` (Date 1 3 2026) `before a repeal or amendment taking effect on` (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Constituents of the printed items (ruling C): the same condition (an offence or breach committed before the day) applies to each.
#ASSERT `repealed or amended legislation continues to have effect as if not repealed or amended for the purpose of` `commencing a proceeding for the offence or breach` `for an offence or breach committed on` (Date 28 2 2026) `before a repeal or amendment taking effect on` (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `repealed or amended legislation continues to have effect as if not repealed or amended for the purpose of` `commencing a proceeding for the offence or breach` `for an offence or breach committed on` (Date 1 3 2026) `before a repeal or amendment taking effect on` (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `repealed or amended legislation continues to have effect as if not repealed or amended for the purpose of` `completing a proceeding for the offence or breach` `for an offence or breach committed on` (Date 28 2 2026) `before a repeal or amendment taking effect on` (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `repealed or amended legislation continues to have effect as if not repealed or amended for the purpose of` `completing a proceeding for the offence or breach` `for an offence or breach committed on` (Date 1 3 2026) `before a repeal or amendment taking effect on` (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `repealed or amended legislation continues to have effect as if not repealed or amended for the purpose of` `imposing a penalty for the offence or breach` `for an offence or breach committed on` (Date 28 2 2026) `before a repeal or amendment taking effect on` (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `repealed or amended legislation continues to have effect as if not repealed or amended for the purpose of` `imposing a penalty for the offence or breach` `for an offence or breach committed on` (Date 1 3 2026) `before a repeal or amendment taking effect on` (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `repealed or amended legislation continues to have effect as if not repealed or amended for the purpose of` `imposing any other remedy or relief for the offence or breach` `for an offence or breach committed on` (Date 28 2 2026) `before a repeal or amendment taking effect on` (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `repealed or amended legislation continues to have effect as if not repealed or amended for the purpose of` `imposing any other remedy or relief for the offence or breach` `for an offence or breach committed on` (Date 1 3 2026) `before a repeal or amendment taking effect on` (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `repealed or amended legislation continues to have effect as if not repealed or amended for the purpose of` `making an order for the offence or breach` `for an offence or breach committed on` (Date 28 2 2026) `before a repeal or amendment taking effect on` (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `repealed or amended legislation continues to have effect as if not repealed or amended for the purpose of` `making an order for the offence or breach` `for an offence or breach committed on` (Date 1 3 2026) `before a repeal or amendment taking effect on` (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `repealed or amended legislation continues to have effect as if not repealed or amended for the purpose of` `giving an order for the offence or breach` `for an offence or breach committed on` (Date 28 2 2026) `before a repeal or amendment taking effect on` (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `repealed or amended legislation continues to have effect as if not repealed or amended for the purpose of` `giving an order for the offence or breach` `for an offence or breach committed on` (Date 1 3 2026) `before a repeal or amendment taking effect on` (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `repealed or amended legislation continues to have effect as if not repealed or amended for the purpose of` `making a direction for the offence or breach` `for an offence or breach committed on` (Date 28 2 2026) `before a repeal or amendment taking effect on` (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `repealed or amended legislation continues to have effect as if not repealed or amended for the purpose of` `making a direction for the offence or breach` `for an offence or breach committed on` (Date 1 3 2026) `before a repeal or amendment taking effect on` (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `repealed or amended legislation continues to have effect as if not repealed or amended for the purpose of` `giving a direction for the offence or breach` `for an offence or breach committed on` (Date 28 2 2026) `before a repeal or amendment taking effect on` (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `repealed or amended legislation continues to have effect as if not repealed or amended for the purpose of` `giving a direction for the offence or breach` `for an offence or breach committed on` (Date 1 3 2026) `before a repeal or amendment taking effect on` (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `repealed or amended legislation continues to have effect as if not repealed or amended for the purpose of` `another purpose` `for an offence or breach committed on` (Date 28 2 2026) `before a repeal or amendment taking effect on` (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Section 35 -- Powers exercised under repealed or amended legislation have continuing effect`

-- src:272 | 35 Powers exercised under repealed or amended legislation have continuing effect
-- src:273 | Anything done in the exercise of a power under repealed or amended legislation, and that is in effect immediately before that repeal or amendment, continues to have effect as if it had been exercised under any other legislation—
-- src:274 | that, with or without modification, replaces, or that corresponds to, the legislation repealed or amended; and
-- src:275 | under which the power could be exercised.
#ASSERT `a thing done in the exercise of a power continues to have effect as if exercised under the other legislation` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `a thing done in the exercise of a power continues to have effect as if exercised under the other legislation` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `a thing done in the exercise of a power continues to have effect as if exercised under the other legislation` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `a thing done in the exercise of a power continues to have effect as if exercised under the other legislation` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `a thing done in the exercise of a power continues to have effect as if exercised under the other legislation` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Section 36 -- Legislation made under repealed legislation has continuing effect`

-- src:276 | 36 Legislation made under repealed legislation has continuing effect
-- src:277 | Any legislation made under repealed legislation, and that is in force immediately before that repeal, continues in force as if it had been made under any other legislation—
-- src:278 | that, with or without modification, replaces, or that corresponds to, the legislation repealed; and
-- src:279 | under which it could be made.
-- src:280 | Legislation that continues in force may be amended or revoked as if it had been made under the legislation that replaces, or that corresponds to, the repealed legislation.
#ASSERT `legislation made under repealed legislation continues in force as if made under the other legislation` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `legislation made under repealed legislation continues in force as if made under the other legislation` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `legislation made under repealed legislation continues in force as if made under the other legislation` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `legislation made under repealed legislation continues in force as if made under the other legislation` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `legislation made under repealed legislation continues in force as if made under the other legislation` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `legislation may be amended or revoked as if made under the replacing legislation` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `legislation may be amended or revoked as if made under the replacing legislation` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Section 37 -- How to apply references to new legislation that is not yet in force`

-- src:281 | 37 How to apply references to new legislation that is not yet in force
-- src:282 | This section applies if legislation (new legislation)—
-- src:283 | is to replace (with or without modification), or is to correspond to, existing legislation; and
-- src:284 | is not yet in force.
-- src:285 | A reference in legislation to the new legislation is, until that new legislation comes into force, a reference to the whole or the corresponding part of the existing legislation.
-- Replacing legislation not yet in force (no date yet): the reference is to the existing legislation.
#ASSERT `what a reference to new legislation is a reference to on` (Date 31 5 2026) `when the new legislation replaces or corresponds to existing legislation` TRUE `and comes into force` NOTHING EQUALS JUST `The whole or the corresponding part of the existing legislation`
-- With a date: until it comes into force (the day before is before; the day itself is not).
#ASSERT `what a reference to new legislation is a reference to on` (Date 31 5 2026) `when the new legislation replaces or corresponds to existing legislation` TRUE `and comes into force` (JUST (Date 1 6 2026)) EQUALS JUST `The whole or the corresponding part of the existing legislation`
#ASSERT `what a reference to new legislation is a reference to on` (Date 1 6 2026) `when the new legislation replaces or corresponds to existing legislation` TRUE `and comes into force` (JUST (Date 1 6 2026)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `what a reference to new legislation is a reference to on` (Date 2 6 2026) `when the new legislation replaces or corresponds to existing legislation` TRUE `and comes into force` (JUST (Date 1 6 2026)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not replacing or corresponding to existing legislation: the section does not apply.
#ASSERT `what a reference to new legislation is a reference to on` (Date 31 5 2026) `when the new legislation replaces or corresponds to existing legislation` FALSE `and comes into force` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 38 -- How to apply references to repealed legislation`

-- src:286 | 38 How to apply references to repealed legislation
-- src:287 | The repeal of legislation does not affect legislation in which the repealed legislation is applied, incorporated, or referred to.
-- src:288 | A reference in legislation to repealed legislation is a reference to legislation that, with or without modification, replaces, or that corresponds to, the legislation repealed.
-- src:289 | Subsection (1) is subject to subsection (2).
#ASSERT `what a reference in legislation to repealed legislation is` TRUE EQUALS `The reference is a reference to the legislation that replaces, or corresponds to, the legislation repealed`
#ASSERT `what a reference in legislation to repealed legislation is` FALSE EQUALS `The legislation that refers to the repealed legislation is unaffected by the repeal`
